  "facts": [
    "Abernethy Bridge, a steel plate and box girder marvel, opened May 28, 1970, after a $17.1 million construction boom that began in 1968 and pushed the new I‑205 route across the Willamette.",
    "The 2,727‑foot span features 15 segments and 60 girders, with a 430‑foot central span flanked by 300‑foot spans, delivering six lanes—three each direction—through Oregon City and West Linn.",
    "A seismic retrofit from 2000 to 2002 cost $7 million, and in 2009 the Oregon Department of Transportation repaved the roadway, replacing expansion joints to keep the bridge safe for 95,500 daily commuters."
  ],
